{
 "note": "Hand-adjudicated glass annotations over the go2 replays. Candidates come from Yoloe2DDetector (PROMPT mode, 'glass wall'/'glass door'/'window'/'glass partition') on the camera stream; the pane is placed in world coordinates by casting rays through the segmentation mask's bottom edge onto the floor plane measured by the lidar (cv2.fisheye + the go2 front_camera_720.yaml intrinsics and BASE_TO_OPTICAL mount). A human confirmed or rejected each one from the camera frame. verdict is one of glass / notglass / unsure. learnable marks panes that leave a trace in the point cloud (>=30 returns on the pane, >=30% of its width covered, <=3.5 m range, flanking structure) -- only those can appear in an eval, since an encoding cannot report a surface that returned nothing. Box bearing carries a systematic error of a few degrees from the camera mount; ~5-15 cm at these ranges, which does not change any verdict.",
